From 844f323569e87d61ce7ab8ab1a35c27b5fc43469 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 11:40:19 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] kanban sync fake: validate release
 failure_limit/block_kind/run_uid as releaseTask

FakeService.release_inputs now models releaseTask's post-fence policy checks
(transitions.ts releaseTask): failure_limit, when present, must be
Number(value) a positive safe integer (explicit null is 0 and refused), and
block_kind (op.block_kind ?? "transient") must be transient | assignment |
capability. Both run after fence() and before the extra/diagnostic checks, so
a spawn_failed release with a bad policy is `invalid` instead of the fake's
NotImplementedError. The "not modelled" caveat is gone.

release_op and the FakeHub leases route also model releaseTask's run_uid
presence check, which runs before fence(): a missing or null run_uid is
`invalid` (release_op raised KeyError before).

Tests (tests/hermes_cli/test_kanban_sync_rejections.py):
- bad failure_limit / block_kind -> invalid, no state change, for every
  outcome incl. spawn_failed, on both release routes;
- accepted policy values (JS coercion of "3", true, null block_kind);
- missing/null run_uid -> invalid, no state change, incl. spawn_failed;
- spawn_failed fence arms: missing lease, other holder, stale run_uid ->
  lease_lost before any input check, on both routes (review 5890134554).

Follow-up of PR #2078 reviews 5889317079 and 5890134554 (test-only).
